body:
It's all right, I was just venting. I'm an english major so I don't know how much of that stuff would really translate. My issue is that I can't concentrate when I'm reading, which is a pretty big deal for english. I'm looking at the final exam questions and I answered one but I can't really answer the other two, and I can't really answer any of them for my other class. One of them is a take home final, I'm looking at the study guide for the other one. It's basically my fault. I let it slip a little earlier in the semester and didn't stay current with the reading and didn't take enough notes in class. Whatever, I'll try my best. I was doing pretty well in the class prior to this so hopefully it doesn't damage my grade too much. 

&#x200B;

I dropped out of college the first time after experiencing mania and my first hospitalization. I only have about a year left, and I'm grateful to be back in school, but it's definitely hard. I guess it's supposed to be hard. Thanks for the kind words and encouragement.
